{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured `/usr/local/bin/os-comparison-worker` as the enabled `inventory-worker` systemd service on node1. It runs under the dedicated locked `inventorysvc` account and recovered successfully after a full node restart. RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 remain unchanged.","actions_performed":["Created the `inventorysvc` system account with no home, a locked password, and `/sbin/nologin`.","Installed and enabled a hardened SELinux-labeled `inventory-worker.service` unit.","Verified the running process uses the expected unprivileged UID/GID and has `NoNewPrivileges` enabled.","Restarted node1 safely and verified boot identity changed and the service automatically recovered.","Installed no additional software and left the system healthy with no failed units."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Run the worker as managed service `inventory-worker` under `inventorysvc`","command_ids":["cmd-2c00a8447ae2473b","cmd-d8e2efb517d44249","cmd-76315f20cea34905","cmd-eaa43f860a904377"],"summary":"The dedicated account exists; the service is enabled and active; its live process runs with UID/GID 992 matching inventorysvc; the account is locked and uses nologin."},{"requirement":"Preserve the installed operating-system release and kernel and use compatible native service management","command_ids":["cmd-032e22c01c4643d4","cmd-40403f10f880432c"],"summary":"Before and after configuration, node1 reports RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64. The native systemd unit passes verification."},{"requirement":"Apply security and reliability controls","command_ids":["cmd-76315f20cea34905","cmd-eaa43f860a904377","cmd-40403f10f880432c"],"summary":"SELinux remains enforcing; unit and executable labels are correct; the service uses no-new-privileges, an empty capability set, protected filesystems/kernel interfaces, restrictive umask, and restart-on-failure."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node1 restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-76315f20cea34905","cmd-65b0e0025adf4531","cmd-28b552ce859442d7","cmd-eaa43f860a904377"],"summary":"Healthy baseline boot ID 368725cb-c64e-4393-b25f-da5111703b4a was captured, reboot acknowledgement returned, post-restart boot ID changed to 0552fbec-93d3-4a3d-b13d-3dc06e94edfb, and the system plus inventory-worker recovered to running/active state."}]}
